# Architecture

- `block/entity`: `DreamTableBlockEntity` is the facade. Its state lives in `MaterialLedger` (delivered and used counts, swaps), `BuildProgress` (phase, step, timer, owner, speed, placed and paid steps), and `FarmPlacement` (anchor and facing).
- `farm`:
  - `FarmBuilder` places one step per call.
  - `FarmDismantler` takes an unfinished build apart on discard.
  - `ObstacleRules` decides what may be cleared.
  - `FarmSpawns` handles mobs and buckets.
  - `MaterialSwaps` lists compatible blocks.
- `farm/schematic`: one reader per format (`VanillaReader`, `SpongeReader`, `LitematicaReader`), driven by `SchematicReader`.
- `farm/legacy`: code-built farms, used only when a bundled `.schem` can't be read.
- `screen`: `DreamTableScreen` only wires things together. `TableButtons` is the server side of every button. Page and button ids are constants in `DreamTableScreenHandler`.
- `screen/page`: one `TablePage` per menu page. `ProjectState` reads the synced phase on the client.
- `screen/ui`: `Theme`, `Painter`, `Viewport`, `SearchBox`.
- `client/clipboard` and `client/hologram`: the world-space board and the ghost blocks.

## Server owns the state
The client only previews with `handler.preview(...)` and sends a button id. `TableButtons` changes the table, and the table calls `sync()`.

## Adding a menu page
1. Add `PAGE_*` and `BUTTON_*` constants in `DreamTableScreenHandler`.
2. Handle the buttons in `TableButtons`.
3. Create a `TablePage` in `screen/page` that draws through `PageContext` (`card`, `button`, `go`).
4. Register the page in `DreamTableScreen.page()`.
